```javascript
let canFlag = isAdminOrModerator || (userReputation >= minimumReputation);

if (targetPrivileged && !reporterPrivileged) {
    canFlag = false;
}
```

But the issue is that `isAdminOrModerator` (or `reporterPrivileged`) is checked FIRST. So if someone is an admin/mod, they can flag regardless of the reputation requirement. But regular users need to meet the reputation requirement.

However, the problem described in the PR is that regular users can't flag at all, and admins can flag unlimited. Let me look at the `src/api/flags.js` to understand the API endpoint.

```bash
cat src/api/flags.js
